<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56029" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατοκωχ-ή</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατοχή</span>
			, <i>possession</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς χώρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anon.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>; <i>mental grasp</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν εἰρημένων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Zeno Stoic.
					1.58
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>being possessed, inspiration</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θείᾳ μοίρᾳ καὶ κατοκωχῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ion</u>
					536c
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπὸ Μουσῶν κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					245a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.174
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Dam.
				<u>Isid.</u>
				32
			</span></i>:—the forms <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατακωχή,
			-ιμος</span> are late and incorrect; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνοκωχή, συνοκωχή</span>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
